<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain holds key rate steady at 5.50 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain holds key rate steady at 5.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain said it left its key money rate unchanged at 5.50 percent at Wednesday's regular repurchase tender for central bank certificates.</p>
<p>It allotted 3.44 trillion pesetas against an equal amount bid.</p>
<p>The central bank last cut the rate by 25 basis points on April 15 to 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
